{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Let the earth bring forth.</b> It is as I explained — that everything was created on the first day, and they needed only to be brought forth." "<b>A living soul.</b> That there is in it vitality." "<b>And creeping things.</b> These are שְׁרָצִים — that they are low and creep along the earth and appear as though dragged, for their walking is not noticeable. Every term רֶמֶשׂ and שֶׁרֶץ in our language is קונמו״בריש בְּלַעַ״ז."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {2 "the la'az appears to correspond to Old French conmovre/rems, terms for creeping or crawling creatures; the reading is uncertain."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:57:08.952728189Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}